# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 3a (partner opens 1S).
title: Partner opens 1♠: raise or not?
id: L02-01
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3
student: S
board: 1
dealer: N
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AQJ75  K84    A5     732
  E  962    J976   JT8    AKT
  S  KT4    A3     9432   J865
  W  83     QT52   KQ76   Q94

auction:
  N 1S     = 13+ points, at least four spades
  E Pass
  S 2S*    = 6-9 points and spade support
     key: 8 HCP plus 1 for the doubleton heart makes 9, and you have three spades. Raise.
     not 1NT: Did you check the list from the top? With three-card support, the raise comes first.
     not Pass: Did you count your points? 8 HCP is enough to respond.
     not 3S: 3♠ shows 12-13 points and four spades. Is your hand that strong?
     not *: With 6-9 points and three spades, can you show partner the fit right away?
  W Pass
  N Pass   = A minimum opening: no game in sight
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 1♠ showed 13+ points and at least four spades, so your three
  spades give your side at least seven, very likely eight. Your 2♠ showed
  6-9 points with support. Partner has a minimum, so even if you have 9,
  your side has about 22: not enough for game. She passes. North is
  declarer, because she bid spades first, and so East will lead to the
  first trick.

play:
  1   E CK  S C5  W C9  N C2
  2   E CA  S C6  W C4  N C3
  3   E CT  S CJ  W CQ  N C7
      note: West's queen takes the third club.
  4   W DK  N DA  E D8  S D2
  5   N H4  E H6  S HA  W H2
      note: Declarer's plan: ruff a heart in dummy, then draw trumps. First the ♥A.
  6   S H3  W H5  N HK  E H7
      note: Back to the ♥K.
  7   N H8  E H9  S S4  W HT
      note: Dummy ruffs the last heart.
  8   S SK  W S3  N S5  E S2
      note: Now draw trumps.
  9   S ST  W S8  N SJ  E S6
      note: Declarer plays the ♠J, or East's ♠9 could win this trick.
  10  N SA  E S9  S D3  W D6
      note: The last trump.
  11  N SQ  E HJ  S D4  W D7
      note: Declarer's trumps are winners.
  12  N S7  E DT  S D9  W HQ
      note: And another.
  13  N D5  E DJ  S C8  W DQ
      note: Only a diamond is left to lose. 9 tricks: 2♠ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: ruff a heart in dummy, then draw trumps. That makes
  six trump tricks, two hearts and a diamond.

  2♠ made with an overtrick. Your raise told partner about the fit at
  once, and the point count told her to stop low.
